1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,440
Which terminal does the processing center expect each debit to come through?

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:07,916
It only accepts debits from terminals it already knows.

3
00:00:07,916 --> 00:00:15,047
So the terminal module keeps a registry: for each sales point and card scheme, one merchant ID and one terminal ID.

4
00:00:15,047 --> 00:00:19,357
Uzcard and Humo payments can use different terminals for the very same shop.

5
00:00:19,357 --> 00:00:23,238
Before every debit, the payment module resolves the terminal.

6
00:00:23,238 --> 00:00:27,702
No active terminal means no debit, and the payment fails closed.

7
00:00:27,702 --> 00:00:32,571
Every terminal change is logged, so an audit can see what was active, and when.

8
00:00:32,571 --> 00:00:36,821
Next, the card schemes themselves: talking to Uzcard and Humo.

